# Copy to .env and fill in. The three model-API settings at the bottom are
# required for step 3; everything else is optional.

# Where runtime files live. Defaults are relative to the project root.
# NEVER commit state.json: it holds live session cookies.
# STATE_PATH=./state.json
# SEARCHES_PATH=./searches.json
# CRITERIA_DIR=./criteria
# JOBS_DB_PATH=./jobs.db

# --- Step 3: the model API (required) -------------------------------------
# This project is an API client. It does not load a model, hold weights or start
# a server: whatever serves the model is yours to run, and these three only say
# where to reach it. Add a `.env` here (it is gitignored) or export them.
#
# LLM_BASE_URL is the OpenAI-compatible root, including the version segment.
# LLM_MODEL is a model id that endpoint understands.
# LLM_API_KEY is the credential.
#
# There is deliberately no default endpoint: pointing the pipeline at a provider
# is meant to be a deliberate act, so a missing value is reported before the first
# request instead of quietly choosing a host for you. All three are required.
#
# LLM_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1
# LLM_API_KEY=sk-...
# LLM_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini
#
# Any OpenAI-compatible endpoint works - OpenRouter, Together, Groq, vLLM,
# Ollama's /v1, or a gateway in front of them. A host that rejects strict
# `json_schema` responses is handled too: the request is retried once in plain
# JSON mode with a worked example of the shape added to the prompt (what DeepSeek
# and similar hosts require), and the reply is validated locally.
#
# --- Optional -------------------------------------------------------------
# How many pending jobs are evaluated at the same time. 1 keeps them strictly
# sequential, which is the polite setting for a rate-limited key; raise it when
# the endpoint tolerates parallel requests.
# LLM_MAX_CONCURRENCY=1
